---
import PageHeader from '../components/ui/PageHeader.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { PAGES } from '../lib/seo';
import { REPOS } from '../lib/site';

const updated = 'November 11, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout {...PAGES['/terms']}>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Terms of use"
    lede="The rules for using this website and the Shetu sync server. The Shetu code itself is free software under the MIT license."
  />

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-[760px] px-5 py-16 sm:px-6 md:py-20">
    <article class="docs-prose">
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <h2>Agreement</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are between you and the Shetu maintainers ("we"). By using
        this website or creating an account on the Shetu sync server we run,
        you agree to them. If you do not agree, do not use the service.
      </p>

      <h2>The software and these terms</h2>
      <p>
        The Shetu desktop app and server are open source under the
        <a href={`${REPOS.monorepo}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>MIT license</a>. That
        license, not these terms, governs how you may use, copy, change and
        share the code. These terms cover the website and the hosted sync
        service. If you run your own server, these terms do not apply to it.
      </p>

      <h2>Your account</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Give accurate sign-in details and keep your password and recovery kit safe.</li>
        <li>You are responsible for what happens under your account.</li>
        <li>Your vault is encrypted with a key only you hold. If you lose both your password and your recovery kit, we cannot recover your data.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>Do not use Shetu to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>break the law or help someone else break it;</li>
        <li>access computers or accounts you are not authorized to access;</li>
        <li>attack, overload, probe or disrupt the service, or get around its rate limits or security;</li>
        <li>use the service in a way that harms other users.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Security research is welcome. Report what you find through
        <a href={`${REPOS.monorepo}/security/advisories/new`}>GitHub Security Advisories</a>
        and do not access other users' data.
      </p>

      <h2>Your data</h2>
      <p>
        What you store in Shetu stays yours. You allow us to store, copy and
        transmit it only to run the service for you and the teams you share
        with. The <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> explains what we
        collect and why.
      </p>

      <h2>Teams</h2>
      <p>
        Team owners and admins decide who joins a team and what is shared with
        it. Anyone you share a vault with can read and copy its contents on
        their own devices, and data already on a removed member's device
        cannot be wiped remotely. Share carefully.
      </p>

      <h2>A free service, provided as is</h2>
      <p>
        The hosted sync service is free and run on a best-effort basis. There
        is no uptime guarantee. We may change, limit, pause or end the service,
        and will try to give notice before ending it. Your data stays in the
        app on your devices, and you can move to your own server at any time.
      </p>
      <p>
        To the extent the law allows, the website, software and service are
        provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any kind,
        including fitness for a particular purpose, availability or freedom
        from errors or data loss. Keep your own backups of anything important.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the extent the law allows, the Shetu maintainers are not liable for
        any indirect, incidental, special or consequential damages, or for lost
        data, profits or access, arising from your use of the website, the
        software or the service. Nothing in these terms limits liability that
        cannot be limited by law.
      </p>

      <h2>Suspension and ending your account</h2>
      <p>
        You can stop using Shetu at any time and ask us to delete your account,
        as described in the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>. We may
        suspend or close accounts that break these terms or put the service or
        other users at risk.
      </p>

      <h2>Other services</h2>
      <p>
        Shetu links to and works with services we do not run, such as GitHub,
        Google sign-in and Cloudflare. Their own terms apply when you use them.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms. When we do, we change the date at the top,
        and the full history stays public in the
        <a href={REPOS.web}>shetu-web repository</a>. Using the service after a
        change means you accept the new terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms go to
        <a href={`${REPOS.monorepo}/issues`}>GitHub Issues</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
